# Line-ending rules for the API subtree, repeated here on purpose.
#
# The release bundle is built with `git archive <commit>:api` — a *subtree*
# archive. Git resolves .gitattributes relative to the tree being archived, so
# the root .gitattributes is invisible to it, and `core.autocrlf=true` on a
# Windows checkout converts every text file on the way out.
#
# That is how api/watchdog.sh reached production with CRLF and died on its first
# line — `set: usage: set [-abefhkmnptuvxBCEHPT]`, then `curl: (3) URL rejected`
# — every minute since it was installed, so the health check that exists to
# notice the API being down had never once checked it.
#
# Verifiable in one line:
#   git archive HEAD api/watchdog.sh | tar -xO | file -    → LF
#   git archive HEAD:api watchdog.sh | tar -xO | file -    → CRLF
#
# api/tests/shellScriptLineEndings.test.js asserts the shipped bundle, not just
# the working tree, so this file cannot quietly stop being applied.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
